WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.819
From sleeper hits like It Comes At Night to
box-office record-breakers like It and Get

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:07.689
Out, 2017 has been a great year for horror.

00:00:07.689 --> 00:00:12.150
But for every high-profile killer clown, there
are a dozen low-key horror movies that slip

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.370
straight onto DVD or — more frequently these
days — video on demand.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:20.840
Here are the under-appreciated horror movies
you may have missed in 2017.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.560
The Devil's Candy

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.830
Mixing heavy metal and horror, The Devil's
Candy follows a struggling artist, played

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:31.929
with an unsettling creepiness by Ethan Embry,
who moves his family out to rural Texas.

00:00:31.929 --> 00:00:35.850
When the previous owner of their new house
starts making sinister nighttime visits, the

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:39.030
family's already turbulent lifestyle descends
into terror.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.430
The Devil's Candy made the rounds at horror
festivals in 2015, but it wasn't until 2017

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:47.720
that the film got a more widespread release
via video-on-demand services.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.850
Written and directed by Sean Byrne, whose
previous film was an equally unique horror

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.710
flick called The Loved Ones, The Devil's Candy
plays with themes from old-school occult films

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.940
while confidently slipping into its own modern
take on the genre.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.040
"Just the gas?"

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.590
The Evil Within

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:12.250
It's impossible to talk about The Evil Within
without mentioning writer-director Andrew

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:16.740
Getty, who spent more than a decade meticulously
crafting this schizophrenic passion project

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.770
before passing away in 2015, two years before
the finished film was released.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:25.360
But he left us with a very well-made, highly
visual horror movie that will surely leave

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.640
viewers with some very specific nightmares.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.560
"Someone like me."

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:34.090
The Evil Within tells the story of a mentally
handicapped man named Dennis, played by Frederick

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:37.590
Koehler, who lives with with his brother,
played by Sean Patrick Flanery.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:41.540
After Dennis's reflection starts telling him
to kill people, things go downhill pretty

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.110
quickly — to put it mildly.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:44.110
"Yeah.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:46.060
Yeah, it's a good way of saying it I guess."

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.200
Berlin Syndrome

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:52.320
Stockholm Syndrome is a disturbing condition
in which someone who's been kidnapped develops

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.200
a sense of affection for their kidnapper.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.420
The film Berlin Syndrome plays with that idea
by following an Australian tourist who has

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:02.430
a one-night stand with a man in Berlin, only
to find herself locked in his apartment.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.570
The struggle that follows is pure psychological
horror that dives deep into the mindset of

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:11.060
survival and the subtleties of psychosis,
all anchored by a phenomenal performance by

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.000
Australian actress Teresa Palmer and a bone-pounding
musical score.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.090
Sometimes touching, sometimes brutal, Berlin
Syndrome is definitely a trip abroad that

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.460
you won't forget anytime soon.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.460
The Blackcoat's Daughter

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:28.350
Writer/director Ox Perkins' slow-burn possession
film The Blackcoat's Daughter was made in

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.540
2015, but didn't secure a release until 2017.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:36.190
Starring American Horror Story's Emma Roberts
and Dexter's James Remar, the film centers

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:40.640
on two girls who are left at their prep school
after the rest of the kids go home for vacation.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.450
It turns out that both girls are hiding a
secret, and events start to spiral out of

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.560
their control in the worst possible way.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.580
If you're looking for a gore-fest filled with
jump scares, you're better off looking elsewhere.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.810
But if you want to spend your night with an
atmospheric horror film that bleeds tension,

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:55.810
queue this one up.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:57.630
"It's fun to be scared sometimes."

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.280
A Dark Song

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.090
You couldn't ask for a more powerful directorial
debut than A Dark Song, and Liam Gavin — who

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:07.890
pulled double duty as both writer and director
on this smart, engaging portrayal of ritual

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:11.060
black magic — is definitely a director to
look for in the future.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:15.480
Gavin crafted a surreal, minimalist film that
may be one of the most technically detailed

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.220
occult movies of the last decade, if not ever.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:22.930
There aren't any jump scares, and very little
blood, but the build-up over A Dark Song's

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:26.830
100-minute runtime is just as satisfying as
the ultimate climax.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.360
Dig Two Graves

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:33.060
Not your typical horror movie, Dig Two Graves
is more of a hardboiled revenge tale.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.670
The story centers on a young girl who makes
a pact with a group of gypsy mountain men

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:40.200
to bring her brother back from the dead — if
she's willing to pay the price.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.670
This indie thriller premiered at the New Orleans
Film Festival in October 2014, then quietly

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:50.209
sat in the shadows until it was released online
in 2017, but it was certainly worth the wait.

00:03:50.209 --> 00:03:55.640
Dig Two Graves blends revenge, thriller, fantasy,
and horror themes into one twisted tale of

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.920
a girl who may have to make the ultimate sacrifice
for her family.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:05.440
"There are no cowards, there are no heroes,
there is only the living and the dead."

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:07.970
Lake Bodom

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:12.490
While it may look like a run-of-the-mill scream-fest,
Lake Bodom's twist is selling itself as a

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:15.880
teen slasher flick when it manages to be so
much more.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.720
If you've never heard of it, don't beat yourself
up.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:22.211
After a short festival run, this Finnish horror
release slipped quietly onto Shudder, a video

00:04:22.211 --> 00:04:26.630
on demand service specializing in horror movies,
virtually ensuring that only a handful of

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.130
people outside of Finland would ever lay eyes
on it.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:33.130
But for horror purists, Lake Bodom is definitely
worth tracking down.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.130
The Void

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:39.281
Jeremy Gillespie and Steven Kostanski first
teamed up to write and direct the 2011 horror

00:04:39.281 --> 00:04:44.501
comedy Father's Day, a neo-grindhouse tribute
to the ultra-violent "exploitation film" genre

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:46.150
that hit its peak the '70s.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:51.810
Their 2017 follow up, The Void, uses the same
genre-specific cues as that film, only this

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.650
time to pay tribute to cult '80s body horror.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:57.050
The Void is messy, weird, and a ton of fun.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:00.871
It focuses on a police officer, played by
Aaron Poole, who finds himself trapped in

00:05:00.871 --> 00:05:03.720
a hospital when mysterious, hooded figures
surround the building.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:08.180
But while staying inside seems safe, he soon
finds that the greatest terror is living in

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:09.639
the bowels of the hospital itself.

00:05:09.639 --> 00:05:14.090
"It's disgusting, like Carrie levels of blood,
like, very gross."

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.650
House on Willow Street

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:19.780
Admittedly one of the weaker entries on this
list, House on Willow Street may fall a bit

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:23.820
short of the mark in pacing, but the premise
and visual design more than make up for its

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:24.820
flaws.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.480
The film is about two crooks who kidnap a
young woman in the hopes of getting a ransom

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:29.840
from her rich father.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.199
Little do they know, their victim is possessed,
and soon she begins to turn the tables on

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:35.340
her kidnappers.

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:39.620
House on Willow Street doesn't do much to
defy genre conventions, but it serves very

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:42.629
well as a bloody fun horror romp for a lazy
evening.

00:05:42.629 --> 00:05:43.949
The Dark Tapes

00:05:43.949 --> 00:05:46.510
At this point, we've had our fill of anthology
films.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:48.650
The fad arguably kicked off with 2012's V/H/S.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:52.180
"It's not haunted, I'm sure there's a reasonable
explanation…"

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.960
Since then, we've had The ABCs of Death, A
Christmas Horror Story, Holidays, and Tales

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:01.690
of Halloween, to name a few.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:06.470
So when an anthology film comes along that
not only exceeds expectations, but shatters

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.530
them completely, it's worth a mention.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:12.650
The Dark Tapes successfully ratchets up the
terror while avoiding all the pitfalls that

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:15.020
have doomed so many other entries in this
genre.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:19.300
If you want to be grossed out by alien monsters
and scared senseless by paranormal visitors,

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.340
The Dark Tapes is the perfect choice.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:26.380
And while we're on the subject of anthologies,
2017's XX is another quality entry in this

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:30.900
genre — and unlike The Dark Tapes, that
one's available on Netflix.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:32.630
"Wow.

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:35.080
That was intense."

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.270
Thanks for watching!

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.770
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:40.830
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

